From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 02:02:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01081/11362] [outer-loop] Unblock conductor pre-test SKIP
 loop: fix 3 bugs in agent-shipped test_experiment_3986 edge-fallbacks test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The conductor SKIP-looped milestone .369 tasks every ~2 min on 'Pre-tests
failing: 1 failed, 108 passed'. Root causes, all in the agent-shipped test
(implementation was correct): (1) replace(...,1) mutated the FIRST fixture
record but asserted on the THIRD (exp3974) — scoped the mutation to the
exp3974 block; (2) same wrong-target bug in the flagged_adversarial assertion;
(3) the finite parses_sequence monkeypatch leaked past its block (monkeypatch
undoes at test END) so the next run hit StopIteration — real functions now
restored after each fault-injection block. 28/28 pass; pre-test gate green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
